--[[
	SignusClips

	Signus's animations, retargeted from the purchased 125+ Animations &
	Weapons Pack (saile stone studios, group 275555347; ids in
	assets/animations/125-pack/AnimationIds.luau). Signus is a four-joint rig
	(Core, Hood, LeftSleeve, RightSleeve) whose hinge frames all line up with
	its RootPart, exactly as an R15 rig's joints line up with its root, so a
	clip's rotations carry straight across:

	  CoreJoint         Root * Waist        (lower and upper torso together)
	  HoodJoint         Neck
	  LeftSleeveJoint   LeftShoulder * half of LeftElbow   (a sleeve is one
	  RightSleeveJoint  RightShoulder * half of RightElbow  piece: the forearm's
	                                                        reach, halved)

	`frames` were baked by playing each published clip on an R15 rig in
	Studio and sampling the engine-evaluated joints at 20 Hz, so every pose,
	easing and marker is the clip's own. Per frame: root position (3), then
	the four rotations above as axis * angle (3 each). `markers` are the
	clip's authored KeyframeMarkers.

	Grimoire clips start and end in the pack's book-holding stance; poses are
	taken relative to it (STANCE), so Signus rests in its own pose and only
	the motion transfers. The two sword clips (AirSlam, UpTilt) are taken
	relative to their own first frame. The core is damped (WEIGHT) because a
	robe that leans like a torso reads as falling over.

	THE TIMELINE. A plan stretches a clip in segments: 0 -> Swing over
	`windup` seconds (the anticipation the telegraph needs), Swing -> Hit at
	the authored speed (the release stays sharp), a `hold` at Hit (a beam that
	keeps firing), then Hit -> end. The server plans an attack this way and
	times its hits from `marks`; every client draws the same plan from the
	SignusClip attribute (encode/decode), so the release lands on the frame
	the damage does.
]]

local Clips = {}

Clips.Rate = 20

-- Relative weight of each retargeted channel. The core's turn about the
-- vertical is damped harder than its lean (coreYaw): a Grimoire caster twists
-- side-on to the target, and a robe that does the same turns its face away.
local WEIGHT = { core = 0.6, coreYaw = 0.3, hood = 0.75, left = 1, right = 1, lift = 1.8 }
Clips.Weight = WEIGHT

-- Light1's first frame: the stance every Grimoire clip begins and ends in.
local STANCE = { 0, -.09, 0, 0, -.72, 0, -.40, .80, .13, 0, .50, -.02, 1.10, -.44, .32 }

